                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2231/95: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sparks</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-29T19:00:00-05:00">December 29, 1936—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>63. The Foreign Office is agreeable to the proposed announcement of intention to
                    negotiate as outlined in paragraph 1 Department’s telegram No. 44, December 24,
                    3 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sparks</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
